  "description": "YUYDAZ crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C40 H54 Dy6 N18 O38 2+,2(N1 O3 1-),10(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy1A (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.512-3.523 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 92.51-100.79°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy6L2(μ3-OH)4(μ2-OH)2(NO3)6(H2O)6]·2NO3·10H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 μ2-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 6 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 6 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
